cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below. Reuse of the code needs the author's written permission (see LICENSE)."
type: software
title: "GSW Lake Explorer: yearly surface water of any lake on Earth, 1984–2021"
date-released: 2026-10-27
authors:
  - family-names: Abbasalizadehrezaei
    given-names: Parisa
    website: "https://risarezaei.github.io"
repository-code: "https://github.com/RisaRezaei/gee-gsw-lake-explorer"
url: "https://risarezaei.projects.earthengine.app/view/gsw-lake-explorer"
license-url: "https://github.com/RisaRezaei/gee-gsw-lake-explorer/blob/main/LICENSE"
abstract: >-
  Google Earth Engine app: click any lake on Earth, or search it by name, to
  see an animation of its yearly JRC Global Surface Water classes, a chart of
  permanent, seasonal and total water area per year, and a comparison of the
  first and last decades. Lake boundaries come from HydroLAKES; years with
  Landsat data gaps are excluded.
keywords:
  - Google Earth Engine
  - JRC Global Surface Water
  - HydroLAKES
  - lakes
  - surface water change
  - Landsat
